  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nShowers and storms will continue across the area today, mainly south \nand east of the Ohio River, as a frontal boundary slowly sags south. \nStorms are not anticipated to be severe, but localized instances of \nflash flooding cannot be completely ruled out.\n\nSouthwesterly flow increases across the area on Saturday out ahead \nof an approaching shortwave. Storms on Saturday will contain heavy \ndownpours, with PW values approaching 2 inches and ample cape, and \nbe overall somewhat slow to move owing to light steering flow. This \nwill bring a renewed threat for flash flooding to the area. WPC has \nupgraded the excessive rainfall risk to a slight across some of the \narea for Saturday to account for this, and a watch may be needed \nwith future packages. Sunday overall should be a bit drier behind \nthe departing wave, however, a front does approach the area towards \nlater in the day, and into Monday, with at least isolated \nshowers/storms anticipated. \n\nNext week looks to start out hot and humid as heights build out \nahead of an approaching front, which will lead to breakdown of the \nridge and increased chances for storms towards mid to late week.",
